.Sh DESCRIPTION
These are the archival applets of BusyBox 1.36.1 as configured for Rach2.
.Bl -tag -width rpm2cpio
.It Nm bunzip2
Decompress bzip2 files, or standard input if no files are given.
.It Nm bzcat
Decompress bzip2 data to standard output.
.It Nm bzip2
Compress files or standard input with the bzip2 algorithm.
It also decompresses with
.Fl d .
.It Nm cpio
Extract or list files from a cpio archive.
It can also read a file list from standard input to create an archive
or copy the files to a directory.
.It Nm dpkg
Install, remove, and manage Debian packages.
Rach2 images contain no dpkg package database.
.It Nm dpkg-deb
List or extract files and control information from Debian packages.
.It Nm gunzip
Decompress gzip files, or standard input if no files are given.
.It Nm gzip
Compress files or standard input.
It also decompresses with
.Fl d .
.It Nm lzcat
Decompress LZMA data to standard output.
.It Nm lzma
Decompress LZMA files or standard input with
.Fl d .
This applet does not compress.
.It Nm lzop
Compress files with lzop, or decompress them with
.Fl d .
.It Nm rpm
Install or query RPM packages.
Rach2 images contain no RPM package database.
.It Nm rpm2cpio
Write the cpio archive from an RPM package to standard output.
.It Nm tar
Create, extract, or list tar archives on the Rach2 file systems.
.It Nm unlzma
Decompress LZMA files, or standard input if no files are given.
.It Nm unxz
Decompress xz files, or standard input if no files are given.
.It Nm unzip
Extract selected files from a ZIP archive.
.It Nm xz
Decompress xz files or standard input with
.Fl d .
This applet does not compress.
.It Nm xzcat
Decompress xz data to standard output.
.It Nm zcat
Decompress gzip data to standard output.
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
.Ss Compression and decompression
The
.Nm bunzip2 ,
.Nm bzip2 ,
.Nm gunzip ,
.Nm gzip ,
.Nm lzma ,
.Nm unlzma ,
.Nm unxz ,
and
.Nm xz
applets accept:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl c
Write to standard output.
.It Fl f
Force the operation.
.It Fl k
Keep input files.
.It Fl t
Test integrity.
.El
.Pp
.Nm bzip2
also accepts
.Fl 1
through
.Fl 9
to select the compression level.
.Fl d
selects decompression for
.Nm bzip2 ,
.Nm gzip ,
.Nm lzma ,
and
.Nm xz .
.Pp
.Nm lzop
accepts:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl 1 No through Fl 9
Select the compression level.
.It Fl d
Decompress.
.It Fl c
Write to standard output.
.It Fl f
Force the operation.
.It Fl U
Delete input files.
.It Fl v
Produce verbose output.
.It Fl C
Also write a checksum of the compressed block.
.It Fl F
Do not store or verify checksums.
.El
.Ss cpio
.Bl -tag -width "--renumber-inodes"
.It Fl t
List archive contents.
.It Fl i
Extract the named
.Ar EXTR_FILE Ns s ,
or all files if none are named.
.It Fl o
Create an archive from the file list on standard input.
Requires
.Fl H Cm newc .
.It Fl p Ar DIR
Copy the files to
.Ar DIR .
.It Fl H Cm newc
Select the newc archive format.
.It Fl d
Create leading directories.
.It Fl m
Restore modification times.
.It Fl v
Produce verbose output.
.It Fl u
Overwrite files.
.It Fl F Ar FILE
Use
.Ar FILE
as input for
.Fl t ,
.Fl i ,
or
.Fl p ,
or as output for
.Fl o .
.It Fl R Ar USER Ns Op : Ns Ar GRP
Set the owner, and optionally group, of created files.
.It Fl L
Dereference symbolic links.
.It Fl 0
Read NUL-terminated input names.
.It Fl Fl ignore-devno
Write zero device numbers in the archive.
.It Fl Fl renumber-inodes
Renumber archive inodes.
.El
.Ss dpkg
.Bl -tag -width "--force-confnew"
.It Fl i , Fl Fl install
Install the package.
.It Fl l , Fl Fl list
List installed packages.
.It Fl C , Fl Fl configure
Configure an unpacked package.
.It Fl P , Fl Fl purge
Remove all files of a package.
.It Fl r , Fl Fl remove
Remove all files except configuration files.
.It Fl u , Fl Fl unpack
Unpack a package without configuring it.
.It Fl F Cm depends , Fl Fl force-depends
Ignore dependency problems.
.It Fl F Cm confnew , Fl Fl force-confnew
Overwrite existing configuration files when installing.
.It Fl F Cm confold , Fl Fl force-confold
Keep existing configuration files when installing.
.El
.Ss dpkg-deb
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl c
List files.
.It Fl f
Print control fields.
.It Fl e
Extract control files to
.Ar DIR ,
which defaults to
.Pa ./DEBIAN .
.It Fl x
Extract files to
.Ar DIR .
There is no default directory.
.It Fl X
Extract files with verbose output.
.El
.Ss rpm
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl i
Install the package.
.It Fl qp
Query the package.
.It Fl qpi
Show package information.
.It Fl qpl
List contents.
.It Fl qpd
List documents.
.It Fl qpc
List configuration files.
.El
.Ss tar
.Bl -tag -width "-f TARFILE"
.It Cm c
Create an archive.
.It Cm x
Extract files.
.It Cm t
List files.
.It Fl f Ar TARFILE
Use the named archive.
.Ql -
means standard input or standard output.
.It Fl C Ar DIR
Change to
.Ar DIR
before the operation.
.It Fl v
Produce verbose output.
.It Fl O
Extract to standard output.
.It Fl m
Do not restore modification times.
.It Fl o
Do not restore user and group ownership.
.It Fl k
Do not replace existing files.
.It Fl z
Use gzip compression or decompression.
.It Fl J
Decompress xz archives.
.It Fl j
Use bzip2 compression or decompression.
.It Fl a
Select compression or decompression by the archive's extension.
.It Fl h
Follow symbolic links.
.It Fl T Ar FILE
Read names to include from
.Ar FILE .
.It Fl X Ar FILE
Read exclusion patterns from
.Ar FILE .
.El
.Ss unzip
.Bl -tag -width "-d DIR"
.It Fl l
List contents; with
.Fl q ,
use the short form.
.It Fl n
Never overwrite files.
The default is to ask.
.It Fl o
Overwrite files.
.It Fl j
Do not restore paths.
.It Fl p
Write to standard output.
.It Fl t
Test the archive.
.It Fl q
Produce less output.
.It Fl K
Do not clear the set-user-ID bit.
.It Fl x Ar FILE
Exclude the named files.
.It Fl d Ar DIR
Extract into
.Ar DIR .
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Extract a Debian package with verbose output:
.Dl dpkg-deb -X ./busybox_0.48-1_i386.deb /tmp
Decompress a gzip file:
.Dl gunzip /tmp/BusyBox-0.43.tar.gz
Compress a tar archive:
.Dl gzip /tmp/busybox.tar
